  "notes": "2025 bulletin - extracted directly from bulletin plan, all courses from scraper's linked_codes. This is NEURO's inaugural appearance in PSU bulletins (2025-2026 catalog); earlier years (2022-2024) show 404 Not Found. Scraper confirms all linked_codes are real (unverified_codes: []). NOTE: Self-verification found scheduling warnings for CHEM courses (CHEM 110/112/113/210/212/213) and BMB 211/BIOL 470 due to unmet prerequisite chains not listed in 2025 bulletin. The 2026 catalog addresses this by explicitly including MATH 3, 4, 21, 22 in the plan. Students using the 2025 plan should confirm prerequisite requirements with advising. QA correction (2026-09-18, reviewer #2): re-scraped the live/archived bulletin and found (a) CHEM 111 (1cr), a real linked code on the bulletin, had been dropped from Semester 1 entirely -- restored. (b) The self-reported CHEM/BMB/BIOL scheduling warnings are real and traced to a genuine hidden prereq chain: CHEM 110 requires MATH 22, which chains back through MATH 21 <- MATH 4 <- MATH 3, none of which the 2025 bulletin's own suggested plan lists (same root cause the pre-existing NEURO-2026.json file already found and fixed for this identical major, and the same fix already used for MATSCI/ME/METEO/MICRB/MINE's identical CHEM 110 gap) -- added MATH 3 (Sem 1), MATH 4 (Sem 2), MATH 21 (Sem 3), MATH 22 (Sem 4) to complete the real chain, and raised max_credits_per_semester to 19 to fit them, mirroring 2026's own precedent and rationale. build_full_plan now reaches 0 warnings for this catalog year. Also found BIOL 470 (Sem 7) needs BIOL 469 as a real prereq, but Sem 5's corresponding item was a generic slot (\"BIOL/BBH 469 or BIOL 4XX (Group A)\") that never actually credits a real completed course to the simulation -- changed it to a real course item (BIOL 469), matching NEURO-2026.json's identical fix. build_full_plan now reaches 0 warnings for 2025.",
